{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Text\/kerning(_:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/openswiftui\/text\/kerning(_:)"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"nonisolated","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"kerning","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"_","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"kerning","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14CoreFoundation7CGFloatV","text":"CGFloat","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI4TextV","text":"Text","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Text","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"parameters":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The spacing to use between individual characters in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"this text. Value of ","type":"text"},{"code":"0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" sets the kerning to the system default value.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"kerning"}],"kind":"parameters"},{"content":[{"anchor":"return-value","type":"heading","text":"Return Value","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Text with the specified amount of kerning.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","text":"Discussion","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Kerning defines the offset, in points, that a text view should shift","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"characters from the default spacing. Use positive kerning to widen the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"spacing between characters. Use negative kerning to tighten the spacing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"between characters.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["VStack(alignment: .leading) {","    Text(\"ABCDEF\").kerning(-3)","    Text(\"ABCDEF\")","    Text(\"ABCDEF\").kerning(3)","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":null},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The last character in the first case, which uses negative kerning,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"experiences cropping because the kerning affects the trailing edge of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the text view as well.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Kerning attempts to maintain ligatures. For example, the Hoefler Text","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"font uses a ligature for the letter combination ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"ffl","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":", as in the word","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"raffle","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":", shown here with a small negative and a small positive kerning:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"ffl","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" letter combination keeps a constant shape as the other letters","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"move together or apart. Beyond a certain point in either direction,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"however, kerning does disable nonessential ligatures.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"important","type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If you add both the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Text\/tracking(_:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"ide